WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.025
The first gate confirms
the authorization boundary.

2
00:00:03.025 --> 00:00:05.751
Check each product on
the FedRAMP Marketplace

3
00:00:05.751 --> 00:00:08.337
on the day you decide,
and record what you read.

4
00:00:08.337 --> 00:00:09.887
As of November 1, 2026,

5
00:00:09.887 --> 00:00:14.625
ServiceNow's Government Community
Cloud is certified at High.

6
00:00:14.625 --> 00:00:17.525
Its commercial cloud has
no listing of its own.

7
00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:21.325
SailPoint Identity Security
Cloud is certified at Moderate.

8
00:00:21.325 --> 00:00:25.075
SailPoint's self-hosted product
has no listing of its own.

9
00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:28.562
Next, confirm what's actually
inside the authorization.

10
00:00:28.562 --> 00:00:33.571
Ask SailPoint in writing whether workflows,
native change detection and the HTTP

11
00:00:33.571 --> 00:00:36.517
request step are in the
authorized environment,

12
00:00:36.517 --> 00:00:38.800
since later gates depend on all three.

13
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.862
Then record which actions
run from a vendor's cloud.

14
00:00:41.862 --> 00:00:46.160
SailPoint's connectors call Microsoft
Graph from SailPoint's cloud,

15
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.950
so each of those calls
is a recorded data flow.

16
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:52.750
And confirm the apps are available
in ServiceNow's government store.
